# Code owners for BacMR/github-security-workflows
#
# Mirrors BacMR/backend's CODEOWNERS so ownership is uniform across the org.
#
# Scope of this file today: it routes review requests automatically and records
# who owns what. It is NOT currently a merge gate -- the `production` ruleset on
# this repo sets require_code_owner_review=false on purpose.
#
# Why that is deliberate: GitHub does not let an author approve their own PR.
# With a single code owner, requiring code-owner review blocks every PR that
# owner opens (this is exactly what blocks BacMR/backend PR #103 today). Turning
# the gate on is a one-line ruleset change once a second owner exists -- add them
# below first, then flip require_code_owner_review.

# Default owner for everything in the repo.
*   @msoueilem

# CI/CD, deploy and security surfaces -- called out explicitly so that a change
# here is never auto-approved by a broader rule added later.
/.github/            @msoueilem
/deploy/             @msoueilem
/.github/CODEOWNERS  @msoueilem
